  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, scVI, ResNet50, transformer, concat) with acc 0.688, but this is a single multimodal result and only modestly better than the best RNA-only model. Image-only evidence is sparse and weak for single-profile ResNet50 (acc 0.208), so it is unclear whether the multimodal gain comes from useful multiprofile image features or from complementary RNA-image fusion. config_012 tests the exact image-side counterpart of config_032 without RNA, isolating the contribution of multiprofile ResNet50 image representation. This is the best next use of budget because it reduces a key uncertainty before committing to more multimodal variants: if image-only multiprofile is weak, it supports the multimodal direction; if it is strong, it redirects attention to image representation/aggregation rather than fusion."
}

